# Machine-local git config.
#
# Git reads ~/.config/git/config (this repo's tracked `gitconfig`, installed
# as a symlink by install.sh) first, then ~/.gitconfig. Any key set here
# overrides the tracked config — not just includeIf routing, but aliases,
# core settings, push/pull defaults, credential helpers, etc.
#
# install.sh creates this file ONLY if it is absent, and never touches it
# again — so nothing here is ever reverted by a re-install.
#
# Common uses:
#   - [includeIf "gitdir:..."] blocks to route identities by directory
#   - Machine-specific credential helpers or signing keys
#   - Overrides for any tracked default (e.g. core.editor, diff.tool)
